title: Checking and reindexing a repository
tags: Storage
kind: guide
summary: mf repo check compares what the store derives with a rebuild; mf repo reindex derives it again.

```
mf -n music repo check       # what no longer holds together; exit code 1 on a problem
mf -n music repo reindex     # derive again what the store derives
```

`check` compares the store's derived key spaces — ids, sets, partitions, the
forest, trigrams, postings — with a rebuild from the primary data, and lists every
difference, one line each (nothing when the store is healthy). It also names the
metarecords an older daemon let hold several positions in one forest: the data is
not damaged, but the daemon no longer means anything by it (spec-data-model "One
position per forest").

`reindex` rebuilds all the derived data from the primary data. Derived data is a
function of the primary data, so reindexing never loses anything; it is the repair
for what `check` reports.

Both hold the repository while they run: other work on it waits.
